 &nbsp; 
 
 
 1 big thing: Air disaster averted 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Flightradar24. Map: Will Jarrett/AP A commercial flight from the UAE to Israel made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia today after one pilot stabbed another, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said .

 Around 170 people were aboard the FlyDubai Boeing 737, which experienced dramatic changes in altitude and ground speed before landing. (See flight data .) The attacking pilot was apparently trying to crash the flight before being subdued by passengers and crew, Netanyahu said — though investigators are still sorting out what happened.

 He added that Saudi officials have arrested the suspected attacker. Their identity has not been released. Passengers from the diverted FlyDubai flight arrive in Israel today. Photo: Jack Guez/AFP via Getty Images FlyDubai said in a statement : "An altercation occurred in the flight deck of flight FZ 1073, operating from Dubai International (DXB) to Ben Gurion International Airport (TLV), on 30 September."

 "The aircraft was successfully secured by on-duty flydubai crew traveling on the flight, who diverted and landed the aircraft safely at Tabuk Airport (TUU). All passengers and crew are safe and accounted for." It remains unclear what motivated the incident, which comes amid high tensions in the Middle East and recalls a largely bygone era of hijackings — especially involving Israeli flights and passengers.

