 2. 🚁 DoorDash unveils delivery drone 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Image: DoorDash DoorDash today unveiled a drone developed for DoorDash Air, its in-house airborne delivery service, Axios' Joann Muller reports. 

 The six-propeller drone was designed around DoorDash's own order data, including the weight and distance of typical orders. 🍕 Harrison Shih, head of DoorDash Air, tells Axios: "We didn't start with a drone and ask what would fit. We started with what people order and how local businesses actually operate, then built the entire system from there."

 The company will begin deliveries in Northern California with restaurants including Chipotle, Popeyes and Momo N Curry. Go deeper . 

 
 
