 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A U.S. Air Force C-130 Hercules prepares for takeoff from Baghdad International Airport yesterday. Photo: Ammar Karim/AFP via Getty Images 🪖 Milestone: The U.S. military announced today that it has withdrawn all American troops from Iraq, ending a 12-year mission to fight the Islamic State. President Trump posted : "Today, I am pleased to announce, that the last American Forces are leaving Iraq! It has been a long time, with very bad decision-making that got us involved in this quagmire in the first place, but soon, that will be part of History." Go deeper . 🏛️ A criminal investigation into allegations that a Cornell University student was gang-raped by seven fraternity members is fueling a new push by House Democratic women to strengthen federal protections against sexual violence on college campuses. More from Kate Santaliz . 🇬🇧 The U.K. has "strong indications" Iran played a part in the incident that saw five men arrested near a U.S.-run military air base in England, Prime Minister Andy Burnham said today. Go deeper . 
 
