 4. 🖼️ 1 for the road: $450M art auction 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Claude Monet's "Le Jardin des Tuileries" is displayed during a preview of the Blaquier-Arrieta Collection. Photo: Ben Bauer/PA via AP A dozen Impressionist and post-Impressionist artworks valued together at almost half a billion dollars are going up for auction after sitting unseen for decades.

 The paintings were owned by the late Argentine art collector Nelly Arrieta de Blaquier and her sugar magnate husband, Carlos Pedro Blaquier. 🎨 They include van Gogh's "Châtaigniers en fleurs" (estimated at $180 million) and Cézanne's "Arlequin" (estimated at $120 million) .

 Neither has been seen in public for half a century. Go deeper . 

 
 
